{"root_cause":"The Checkboxes component only attaches a 'click' event listener, so keyboard interactions (Space/Enter) that trigger a 'change' event do not run the exclusive logic. Additionally, the exclusive logic methods incorrectly select inputs by name attribute rather than by the exclusive group attribute, failing to clear non-exclusive symptom checkboxes when the exclusive checkbox has a different name but shares the same exclusive group.","repair_strategy":"Change the event listener from 'click' to 'change' to capture both mouse and keyboard interactions. Rewrite unCheckAllInputsExcept to select all checkboxes in the same exclusive group (or same name if no group) when an exclusive checkbox is checked. Rewrite unCheckExclusiveInputs to select exclusive checkboxes in the same exclusive group (or same name if no group) when a regular checkbox is checked. Update the handler to use the corrected method logic.","edits":[{"path":"packages/nhsuk-frontend/src/nhsuk/components/checkboxes/checkboxes.js","sha256":"b12e3c7a52e09c981155d2f727c5eb8358d420a487177c9a1e722c19da4c8af0","before":"    // Handle events
    this.$root.addEventListener('click', (event) => this.handleClick(event))
  }","after":"    // Handle events
    this.$root.addEventListener('change', (event) => this.handleChange(event))
  }"},{"path":"packages/nhsuk-frontend/src/nhsuk/components/checkboxes/checkboxes.js","sha256":"b12e3c7a52e09c981155d2f727c5eb8358d420a487177c9a1e722c19da4c8af0","before":"  /**
   * Toggle classes and attributes
   *
   * @param {MouseEvent} event - Click event
   */
  handleClick(event) {
    const $clickedInput = event.target

    // Ignore clicks on things that aren't checkbox inputs
    if (
      !($clickedInput instanceof HTMLInputElement) ||
      $clickedInput.type !== 'checkbox'
    ) {
      return
    }

    // If the checkbox conditionally-reveals some content, sync the state
    const hasAriaControls = $clickedInput.getAttribute('aria-controls')
    if (hasAriaControls) {
      this.syncConditionalRevealWithInputState($clickedInput)
    }

    // No further behaviour needed for unchecking
    if (!$clickedInput.checked) {
      return
    }

    // Handle 'exclusive' checkbox behaviour (ie "None of these")
    if ('checkboxExclusive' in $clickedInput.dataset) {
      this.unCheckAllInputsExcept($clickedInput)
    } else {
      this.unCheckExclusiveInputs($clickedInput)
    }
  }","after":"  /**
   * Handle checkbox state change
   *
   * Runs exclusive logic when a checkbox becomes checked.
   * The change event fires for both mouse and keyboard interactions.
   *
   * @param {Event} event - Change event
   */
  handleChange(event) {
    const $changedInput = event.target

    // Ignore changes on things that aren't checkbox inputs
    if (
      !($changedInput instanceof HTMLInputElement) ||
      $changedInput.type !== 'checkbox'
    ) {
      return
    }

    // If the checkbox conditionally-reveals some content, sync the state
    const hasAriaControls = $changedInput.getAttribute('aria-controls')
    if (hasAriaControls) {
      this.syncConditionalRevealWithInputState($changedInput)
    }

    // No further behaviour needed for unchecking
    if (!$changedInput.checked) {
      return
    }

    // Handle 'exclusive' checkbox behaviour (ie "None of these")
    if ('checkboxExclusive' in $changedInput.dataset) {
      this.unCheckAllInputsExcept($changedInput)
    } else {
      this.unCheckExclusiveInputs($changedInput)
    }
  }"},{"path":"packages/nhsuk-frontend/src/nhsuk/components/checkboxes/checkboxes.js","sha256":"b12e3c7a52e09c981155d2f727c5eb8358d420a487177c9a1e722c19da4c8af0","before":"  /**
   * Uncheck other checkboxes
   *
   * Find any other checkbox inputs with the checkbox group value, and uncheck them.
   * This is useful for when a "None of these" checkbox is checked.
   *
   * @param {HTMLInputElement} $input - Checkbox input
   */
  unCheckAllInputsExcept($input) {
    const { checkboxExclusiveGroup: exclusiveGroup } = $input.dataset

    const allInputsWithSameName = document.querySelectorAll(
      `input[type="checkbox"][name="${$input.name}"]`
    )

    allInputsWithSameName.forEach(($inputWithSameName) => {
      const hasSameFormOwner = $input.form === $inputWithSameName.form

      // Uncheck all with same exclusive group by default, otherwise fall back to
      // GOV.UK Frontend behaviour to uncheck all with the same name attribute
      if (hasSameFormOwner && $inputWithSameName !== $input) {
        this.setInputState($inputWithSameName, false, exclusiveGroup)
      }
    })
  }","after":"  /**
   * Uncheck all other inputs in the same exclusive group (or same name if no group)
   *
   * When an exclusive checkbox (e.g. "None of these") is checked, uncheck all other
   * checkboxes in the same group to enforce mutual exclusivity.
   *
   * @param {HTMLInputElement} $input - Checkbox input that was checked
   */
  unCheckAllInputsExcept($input) {
    const { checkboxExclusiveGroup: exclusiveGroup } = $input.dataset

    let $inputsToUncheck
    if (exclusiveGroup) {
      $inputsToUncheck = $input.form.querySelectorAll(
        `input[type="checkbox"][data-checkbox-exclusive-group="${exclusiveGroup}"]`
      )
    } else {
      $inputsToUncheck = $input.form.querySelectorAll(
        `input[type="checkbox"][name="${$input.name}"]`
      )
    }

    $inputsToUncheck.forEach(($inputToUncheck) => {
      if ($inputToUncheck !== $input) {
        this.setInputState($inputToUncheck, false, exclusiveGroup)
      }
    })
  }"},{"path":"packages/nhsuk-frontend/src/nhsuk/components/checkboxes/checkboxes.js","sha256":"b12e3c7a52e09c981155d2f727c5eb8358d420a487177c9a1e722c19da4c8af0","before":"  /**
   * Uncheck exclusive inputs
   *
   * Find any checkbox inputs with the same checkbox group value and the 'exclusive' behaviour,
   * and uncheck them. This helps prevent someone checking both a regular checkbox and a
   * "None of these" checkbox in the same fieldset.
   *
   * @param {HTMLInputElement} $input - Checkbox input
   */
  unCheckExclusiveInputs($input) {
    const { checkboxExclusiveGroup: exclusiveGroup } = $input.dataset

    const allInputsWithSameNameAndExclusiveBehaviour =
      document.querySelectorAll(
        `input[type="checkbox"][data-checkbox-exclusive][name="${$input.name}"]`
      )

    allInputsWithSameNameAndExclusiveBehaviour.forEach(($exclusiveInput) => {
      const hasSameFormOwner = $input.form === $exclusiveInput.form

      // Uncheck the exclusive input only. When no group is set, fall back to
      // GOV.UK Frontend behaviour and locate the exclusive input by name
      if (hasSameFormOwner) {
        this.setInputState($exclusiveInput, false, exclusiveGroup)
      }
    })
  }","after":"  /**
   * Uncheck exclusive inputs in the same group
   *
   * When a regular checkbox is checked, uncheck any exclusive checkboxes
   * in the same exclusive group (or same name if no group).
   *
   * @param {HTMLInputElement} $input - Checkbox input that was checked
   */
  unCheckExclusiveInputs($input) {
    const { checkboxExclusiveGroup: exclusiveGroup } = $input.dataset

    let $exclusiveInputs
    if (exclusiveGroup) {
      $exclusiveInputs = $input.form.querySelectorAll(
        `input[type="checkbox"][data-checkbox-exclusive][data-checkbox-exclusive-group="${exclusiveGroup}"]`
      )
    } else {
      $exclusiveInputs = $input.form.querySelectorAll(
        `input[type="checkbox"][data-checkbox-exclusive][name="${$input.name}"]`
      )
    }

    $exclusiveInputs.forEach(($exclusiveInput) => {
      if ($exclusiveInput !== $input) {
        this.setInputState($exclusiveInput, false, exclusiveGroup)
      }
    })
  }"}],"expected_accessibility_effect":"Keyboard users can now select the 'No symptoms' exclusive checkbox and have any previously selected symptom checkboxes automatically cleared, satisfying WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard) and 2.4.3 (Focus Order). Mouse clicking continues to work as before.","functional_risks":["The change event fires for programmatic changes, but the handler returns early when the checkbox is unchecked, so no adverse effect is expected.","The new group-based selection might affect other checkbox groups if they share the same group attribute unexpectedly, but the attribute is designed for this purpose.","The swapped method calls could affect any external code calling these methods, but they appear to be private to the component."],"verification_requirements":["Using only the keyboard (Tab to navigate, Space to check), verify that checking cough and fever then checking 'No symptoms' clears cough and fever.","Verify that mouse clicking continues to work as before.","Confirm that conditional reveals linked via aria-controls still synchronize correctly for both mouse and keyboard interactions.","Ensure no errors are thrown when initializing the component on pages that use it.","Verify the regression guard: choosing 'Do not contact me' after ticking a contact method works."]}

reasoning:
The issue is that the Checkboxes component only listens for 'click' events, but keyboard interactions (Space/Enter) trigger 'change' events. The exclusive logic (unchecking other checkboxes when "None of these" is checked) only runs in the click handler, so keyboard users can't clear previously selected symptoms.

Looking at the current code:
1. The constructor attaches a 'click' event listener to `this.$root`
2. The `handleClick` method contains the exclusive logic
3. The `unCheckAllInputsExcept` method selects by name, not by exclusive group
4. The `unCheckExclusiveInputs` method only selects exclusive inputs with the same name

The fix needs to:
1. Change the event listener from 'click' to 'change' to capture both mouse and keyboard interactions
2. Fix the exclusive logic to properly select by exclusive group
3. Ensure the logic works correctly for both exclusive and regular checkboxes

